---
import '../styles/global.css';
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
---

<DocsLayout title="Abel — A small language with clear ideas" description="The Abel programming language documentation and v0.1 language specification.">
  <section class="hero" data-enter>
    <p class="eyebrow">The Abel language · v0.1</p>
    <h1>Small language.<br /><em>Clear ideas.</em></h1>
    <p class="intro">A readable scripting language for small numerical programs. Explore the language contract, then try it from the command line.</p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="button button-dark" href="/specification/">Read the specification <span>↓</span></a>
      <a class="button button-light" href="#about">Why Abel?</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="about" class="principles" aria-label="Language principles">
    <div><span>01</span><strong>Readable</strong><p>Little ceremony, familiar syntax, and behavior designed for beginners.</p></div>
    <div><span>02</span><strong>Useful</strong><p>Scalars, arrays, functions, and a focused numerical standard library.</p></div>
    <div><span>03</span><strong>Stable</strong><p>A deliberately small contract that can grow without breaking existing programs.</p></div>
  </section>

  <section class="documentation-callout">
    <p class="eyebrow">The reference</p>
    <h2>Everything the language promises.</h2>
    <p>The v0.1 specification covers syntax, evaluation, built-ins, arrays, functions, errors, and compatibility policy.</p>
    <a class="text-link" href="/specification/">Open the full specification <span>↗</span></a>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
